  "manual_justification": "Each exposure is the radius-one binary Hamming ball. Distances between 000/001, 001/111 and 000/111 are 1,2,3. Thus graph edges are h0-h1 and h1-h2, but not h0-h2. Record 000 has only true histories h0,h1. Record 011 is shared by h1 and false h2, so global capability is false. Transitive closure adds false h2 to the fibre at 000 even though h2 cannot expose that record.",
